  [1mThe consequence:[0m [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m → [38;5;153m480[39m is a one-line change, but it's a 16× extension of how long a
  session stays valid after the user stops interacting. Concretely:

  - A session on a shared, stolen, or unlocked device stays authenticated for a full working day instead of half an
    hour.
  - A leaked or stolen session token has a 16× larger window to be replayed before it expires on its own.
  - [38;5;153mserver.js:2[39m shows this value is the only thing governing session expiry here — there's no idle-timeout,
    re-auth-on-sensitive-action, or revocation mechanism alongside it to absorb the extra exposure.

  That may be exactly the tradeoff you want (8 hours is a common "don't log me out during the workday" setting). It's
  just not a decision I should make silently on your behalf.

